---
description: Binding rules for graal-delphi (Graal client rebuilds in Delphi)
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow `AGENTS.md` at the repo root on every request. In short:

- Open PRs only; never merge, push to `main`, tag or release.
- One change per branch and PR. Folder PRs touch only their folder (plus
  `common/` when a shared unit really changes) and never the root `README.md`.
- PR bodies start with the attribution block in `AGENTS.md`.
- No original Graal code; game data comes from the player's install. Each
  real exe's embedded resources are extracted per version and wired into
  its own rebuild. No decompile addresses,
  `FUN_`/`DAT_`/`LAB_` names or decompiled C anywhere.
- Test only against loopback servers you start (seihai-gserver, `scripts/relay98.py`).
- `scripts/build.sh` and `scripts/test.sh` must pass with no unfreed memory.
- Each fix: a bullet under the current version's "What's new" in the
  folder's `RELEASE_NOTES.md`, and tick its `- [ ]` item in the folder
  README, `ROADMAP.md` and the issue.
- All clients release together via `release-all.yml`; no per-folder releases.
- Match each folder against its own real client only.

Context: `HANDOFF-CURSOR.md`, `ROADMAP.md`, issue #99.
